{
 "enum": "SpellEffect.Effect handler modes",
 "description": "When each effect runs on the Epsilon core, read off SpellEffects.cpp: the handler table maps an effect to its handler, and the handler's first line names the modes it runs in. LAUNCH and LAUNCH_TARGET run at the cast or after LaunchDelay, HIT once at the landing, HIT_TARGET per target hit; an effect whose handler is EffectNULL or EffectUnused has no handler at all and is `unimplemented`. `phase` is the pack's own reading: an effect that only runs at launch sits at the launch phase whatever the spell's speed, and every other effect lands where the spell does; the damage and heal handlers only accumulate at launch and deal at the hit, so for the phase they land.",
 "source": [
  "https://github.com/EpsilonRP/TrinityCore/blob/master/src/server/game/Spells/SpellEffects.cpp"
 ],
